    53	docs/research/w033-provenance-astra.md:33:1. **Ruling.** The opus branch owns the **entire in-flight opus record**, including state, handoff, reviews, certificates, and their committed evidence. Master owns the filed baseline and, after integration, the accepted record. This is a split by lifecycle phase, never by field. The reviewer produces and records the verdict in an isolated worktree based on the opus branch; that original evidence joins the same branch before its PR lands. Separate bookkeeping PRs must not update an in-flight opus. GitHub’s PR requirement establishes the route to master, not ownership: two PRs can still carry competing records. This ruling extends the branch-ref contract already established in [merge](/home/edckt/projects/bisellium/packages/cli/src/branch.ts:87).
